<title>CANADA: Saskatchewan Ag sees high canola pest risk in 1997.</title>
<headline>Saskatchewan Ag sees high canola pest risk in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's canola fields may face a high threat from flea beetles next spring if the Prairies see a heavy snowfall that protects the insects from the cold, Saskatchewan Agriculture entomologist Lloyd Harris said.</p>
<p>&quot;If a good snowfall puts a blanket over the ground, we should see a lot of flea beetles in 1997,&quot; Harris said in a statement.</p>
<p>Any producers who noticed large numbers of flea beetles this fall should consider using insecticidal seed dressing and granules, he said.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
